    <Placemark>
      <name>Ludington State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Big_Sable_Point_Lighthouse2.JPG/330px-Big_Sable_Point_Lighthouse2.JPG" width="320"/><br/><p>Ludington State Park is a public recreation area located two miles north of Ludington, Michigan, occupying 4,800 acres (1,900 ha) between the shores of Lake Michigan and Hamlin Lake. The state park is crossed by a one-mile stretch of the Big Sable River and is home to the 112-foot-high (34 m) Big Sable Point Lighthouse, which dates from 1876.</p><p>County: Mason</p><p><a href="https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/Ludington">More information</a></p>]]></description>
