    <Placemark>
      <name>Lake Gogebic State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Boardwalk_at_Lake_Gogebic_State_Park_%2829940616062%29.jpg/330px-Boardwalk_at_Lake_Gogebic_State_Park_%2829940616062%29.jpg" width="320"/><br/><p>Lake Gogebic State Park is a public recreation area covering 360 acres (150 ha) in the Upper Peninsula of Michigan. The state park sits on the western shore of Lake Gogebic, the largest inland lake in the Upper Peninsula. The land around the park is sparsely populated, and relatively flat.</p><p>County: Gogebic</p><p><a href="https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/LakeGogebic">More information</a></p>]]></description>
