    <Placemark>
      <name>Palms Book State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Palms_Book_State_Park_%28Kitch-iti-kipi%29.jpg/330px-Palms_Book_State_Park_%28Kitch-iti-kipi%29.jpg" width="320"/><br/><p>Palms Book State Park is a publicly owned nature preserve encompassing 388 acres (157 ha) in Thompson Township, Schoolcraft County, in the eastern Upper Peninsula of Michigan. The state park is noted for Kitch-iti-kipi, the &quot;Big Spring&quot;.</p><p>County: Schoolcraft</p><p><a href="https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/PalmsBook">More information</a></p>]]></description>
