    <Placemark>
      <name>Tawas Point State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Tawaspoint3.jpg/330px-Tawaspoint3.jpg" width="320"/><br/><p>Tawas Point State Park is a public recreation area located on Lake Huron in Northern Michigan near the city of East Tawas, Michigan. The state park encompasses 183 acres (74 ha) at the end of a sand spit that forms Tawas Bay. It has been referred to as the &quot;Cape Cod of the Midwest&quot; and is a notable bird-watching site. The park is home to the Tawas Point Light, which, although it has been remodeled several times, serves as the sole representative of a true Victorian-era style station built on the Great Lakes.</p><p>County: Iosco</p><p><a href="https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/TawasPoint">More information</a></p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#state_park</styleUrl>
