    <Placemark>
      <name>Burt Lake State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Burtlakesp.jpg/330px-Burtlakesp.jpg" width="320"/><br/><p>Burt Lake State Park is a public recreation area covering approximately 125 acres (51 ha) on the south shore of Burt Lake at Indian River in Cheboygan County, Michigan. The state park features 2,000 feet (610 m) of sandy shoreline, swimming and boating access to the Inland Lakes Waterway, fishing on the Sturgeon River and Burt Lake, and camping facilities.</p><p>County: Cheboygan</p><p><a href="https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/BurtLake">More information</a></p>]]></description>
