    <Placemark>
      <name>Baraga State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/BaragaStateParkEntranceSign.jpg/330px-BaragaStateParkEntranceSign.jpg" width="320"/><br/><p>Baraga State Park is a public recreation area covering 56 acres (23 ha) on the shore of Lake Superior's Keweenaw Bay in Baraga County, Michigan. The state park sits along Route 41 on the south side of the village of Baraga. The park, village, and county bear the name of Bishop Frederic Baraga.</p><p>County: Baraga</p><p><a href="https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/Baraga">More information</a></p>]]></description>
