    <Placemark>
      <name>Kal-Haven Trail State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Kal-Haven_Trail.jpg/330px-Kal-Haven_Trail.jpg" width="320"/><br/><p>The Kal-Haven Trail, formally known as the Kal-Haven Trail Sesquicentennial State Park, is a rail trail in the US that originally ran 33.5 miles (53.9 km) between South Haven, Michigan, to a point just west of the city of Kalamazoo, Michigan, where there is a trailhead. In 2008, the trail was extended east from the trailhead to downtown Kalamazoo as part of the Kalamazoo River Valley Trail.</p><p>County: Kalamazoo</p><p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kal-Haven_Trail">More information</a></p>]]></description>
