    <Placemark>
      <name>Laughing Whitefish Falls State Park</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Laughingwhitefish013.jpg/330px-Laughingwhitefish013.jpg" width="320"/><br/><p>Laughing Whitefish Falls State Park is a public recreation area protecting 960 acres (390 ha) along the Laughing Whitefish River in Onota Township and Rock River Township, in far western Alger County, Michigan. Its main scenic feature is Laughing Whitefish Falls, a 100-foot fan-shaped cascade located in the southern part of the site, in Rock River Township, eight miles (13 km) south of Lake Superior and three miles north of M-94.</p><p>County: Alger</p><p><a href="https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/LaughingWhitefish">More information</a></p>]]></description>
